Create and manage service accounts.

{{#bold}}USAGE{{/bold}}
  $ {{#cyan}}axway{{/cyan}} {{#cyan}}service-account{{/cyan}} [--no-banner] [--no-color] [--profile <value>]

{{#bold}}GLOBAL FLAGS{{/bold}}
  {{#cyan}}--no-banner{{/cyan}}        Disable the banner.
  {{#cyan}}--no-color{{/cyan}}         Disable color output.
  {{#cyan}}--profile={{#underline}}<value>{{/underline}}{{/cyan}}  Specify the configuration profile to use.

{{#bold}}DESCRIPTION{{/bold}}
  Create and manage service accounts.

  Create and manage service accounts, generate public/private keypairs, and assign teams.

  When authenticating using a service account in a headless environment, such as a SSH terminal, you must set the token store type to "file":

    axway config set auth.tokenStoreType file

  Available roles can be viewed using the 'roles' subcommand.

{{#bold}}EXAMPLES{{/bold}}
  List all service accounts

    $ axway service-account list

  Create a service account with interactive prompting

    $ axway service-account create

  Create a service account with minimum non-interactive arguments

    $ axway service-account create --name foo --secret bar

  Change a service account name, description, and role

    $ axway service-account update <name/client-id> --name <new_name> --desc <desc> --role <role>

  Add a team to an existing service account

    $ axway service-account add-team <client-id/name> <team_guid> <team_role>

  Remove a team from a service account

    $ axway service-account remove-team <client-id/name> <team_guid>

  Remove a service account

    $ axway service-account remove <client-id/name>

  View available team roles

    $ axway service-account roles

{{#bold}}COMMANDS{{/bold}}
  {{#cyan}}service-account add-team{{/cyan}}          Add a team to a service account.
  {{#cyan}}service-account create{{/cyan}}            Create a service account.
  {{#cyan}}service-account generate-keypair{{/cyan}}  Create a pem formatted public/private key pair.
  {{#cyan}}service-account list{{/cyan}}              List all service accounts.
  {{#cyan}}service-account remove{{/cyan}}            Remove a service account.
  {{#cyan}}service-account remove-team{{/cyan}}       Remove a team from a service account.
  {{#cyan}}service-account roles{{/cyan}}             View available service account roles.
  {{#cyan}}service-account update{{/cyan}}            Update a service account.
  {{#cyan}}service-account view{{/cyan}}              View service account details.

